  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low-bias: model underpredicts during rising regimes (true often +1 to +3 EUR above forecast for ~day 5–25). Apply an upward level shift when the last 5–10 days show a positive slope.",
    "Trend/lag error: forecasts react too slowly to breakouts; peaks occur ~1–3 days later in the model and with smaller amplitude. If price breaks above the 10–15d range, accelerate the path upward (front-load gains).",
    "Underestimated volatility on upside: during rallies, the model caps highs (misses 72–73 area) and keeps forecasts clustered ~68–70. Increase upside variance/allow higher maxima when recent realized range expands.",
    "Late-horizon overshoot after regime change: when the true market turns down (late July/early Aug), the model sometimes stays too high or predicts a delayed spike. Add stronger mean-reversion / downward adjustment beyond ~20–30d when momentum turns negative.",
    "Horizon structure: near-term (1–5d) errors are smaller; mid-horizon (7–20d) shows largest underprediction in uptrends; far-horizon (20–30d) tends to revert too much or overshoot depending on the latest swing. Use regime-dependent corrections by horizon (uptrend: add more mid-horizon uplift; downtrend: add more far-horizon decay)."
  ]
}
